<title>NETHERLANDS: Western primary nickel output steady in Jan - INSG.</title>
<headline>Western primary nickel output steady in Jan - INSG.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western world primary nickel production remained steady at 61,400 tonnes in January, only 200 tonnes above December's monthly total, the International Nickel Study Group said in its latest bulletin.</p>
<p>Canada boosted output to 12,400 tonnes, up from 11,600 in December, and Japan's production stayed strong at 11,400 tonnes against 11,200.</p>
<p>Countering these rises, Australian production dipped to 5,900 tonnes from 7,100 and European output was largely flat.</p>
<p>On the consumption side, western world offtake was little changed at 75,800 tonnes from 75,600, INSG said.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
